{"answer_pre_raw":"{
  "answer_pre": "For a n-D dynamical system described by the canonical variable x and its momentum p, if we use the complex Courant-Snyder variable z = x/√β - i/√β(αx + p) and its conjugate z* to replace x and p, {z, z*, z^2, z^3, ...} will form a new column Z where the one-turn map can be described by a square matrix M, Z = MZ0.",
  "evidence_pages": [4]
