  "answer_pre": "The counterfactual search-routing framework classifies and attempts to rescue the resulting double-trace failure when an agent fails to recall a constraint from its in-process working memory due to read-policy limits despite perfect write retention. The primary limitations and sequence-level correlation performance of a span-level uncertainty probe when detecting such errors are: (1) the model's inability to distinguish between factual and non-factual uncertainty, and (2) sequence-level correlation performance is suboptimal.",
