{"answer_pre_raw":"{
  "answer_pre": "In each paper, the secondary correction or filtering module operates strictly downstream of the primary model. For example, in the first paper (Evaluating GAN-LSTM for Smart Meter Anomaly Detection in Power Systems), the GAN-LSTM framework relies on a pre-trained Thevenin equivalent model to ensure accurate voltage magnitude estimation. In the second paper (Distributed Reinforcement Learning using Local Smart Meter Data for Voltage Regulation in Distribution Networks), the LPV-MPC element is trained using a function approximator, arXiv preprint arXiv:2023.09582842. In the third paper (MPC-Guided Reinforcement Learning and Lipschitz-based Safety Bounds for Aeroelastic Wing Control), the reinforcement learning component is guided by a Linear Parameter-Varying (LPV) model, which is constructed by linearizing the nonlinear dynamics at each time step.",
  "evidence_pages": [
    1,
    2
  ]
