  "answer_pre": "The first paper uses a dual-channel decision framework to distinguish between point outliers and concept drifts, the second paper employs a generalized mixed Laplace distribution regression model to handle heteroskedasticity and asymmetry, and the third paper proposes a mixed-effects longitudinal distribution regression model based on the asymmetric Laplace distribution.",
  "evidence_pages": [1, 2, 3]
}
