{"answer_pre_raw":"```json
{
  "answer_pre": "Each paper uses a distinct, principled stabilization mechanism to control added flexibility: (1) Physics-Informed Singular-Value Learning for cross-covariance forecasting, (2) Two-Stream NN for cross-correlation estimation, and (3) Bayesian Robust Financial Trading with Adversarial Synthetic Market Data. The first mechanism targets non-stationary empirical cross-correlations, the second targets cross-correlations in high-dimensional time series, and the third targets robust trading with synthetic market data.",
