{
  "answer_pre": "MACRO-LLM, Speech-Hands, and SC-MAS all reduce collaboration overhead relative to naive baselines. MACRO-LLM decomposes the spatiotemporal coordination problem into three synergistic modules: CoProposer, Negotiator, and Introspector. Speech-Hands employs a directed acyclic graph (DAG) structure to model agent collaboration. SC-MAS generalizes to heterogeneous multi-agent systems by constructing a directed acyclic graph (DAG) topology.",
  "evidence_pages": [
    1,
    2
  ]
}
