  "answer_pre": "ALDRM would fail to capture heteroskedasticity if the data exhibits strong non-stationarity or extreme spatial discontinuities, while RLGP would fail if the heterogeneity arises from abrupt changes in the data that are not captured by the nearest-neighbor selection process. This reveals that ALDRM assumes homogeneity over the entire longitudinal series, whereas RLGP assumes homogeneity within the selected nearest-neighbor subset around a test point.",
  "evidence_pages": [
    "Doc 1",
    "Doc 2"
  ]
