  "answer_pre": "The in-browser assistant's cold-start solution uses a compact Multi-Layer Perceptron (MLP) trained on clustered sessions from the AOL query log dataset to provide immediate value. The comparative study platform's participant assignment mechanism uses a \"Duplicate Study\" feature for between-subject designs and a \"Condition\" element for within-subject designs. To fairly evaluate personalization effectiveness, the researcher must use the \"Duplicate Study\" design to compare distinct groups of participants (e.g., \"Persona-Adapted\" vs. generic models) with different backends.",
