{"answer_pre_raw":"{
  "answer_pre": "In the first paper (Doc 1), the outlier phenomenon occurs when the spectral radius of the Bell-CHSH operator is 2, and the structural feature causing this is when the orthogonal projections P and Q are not in general position. In the second paper (Doc 2), the outlier phenomenon occurs for the infinite dihedral group D_∞ when τ(z) ∈ [-1, 1], and the structural feature causing this is that the algebraic variety Γ_n converges to the critical variety {z ∈ C^4 : z_0 + z_1 + 2z_2z_3 = 0}.",
  "evidence_pages": [
    3,
    4
  ]
