{"answer_pre_raw":"{
  "answer_pre": "The mathematical criteria for diagnosing integrable versus chaotic behavior in bulk operator evolution fundamentally differ from the criteria for determining admissible integrable boundary conditions in that they probe different aspects of the system's structure: the former focuses on the behavior of the bulk operator under time evolution, while the latter examines the compatibility of the system with integrable boundary conditions.",
  "evidence_pages": ["Doc 1", "Doc 2", "Doc 3"]
