{"answer_pre_raw":"```json
{
  "answer_pre": "Doc 1 introduces a mixed-effects distributional regression model based on the asymmetric Laplace distribution (ALDRM) that handles heteroskedasticity by modeling location, scale, and skewness parameters as functions of explanatory variables and subject-specific random effects. Doc 2 proposes a robust Local Gaussian Process (RLGP) for high-dimensional nonstationary and discontinuous response surfaces, using a mean-shift regularization technique combined with multivariate perspective transformation to manage outliers and abrupt changes.",
