{"answer_pre_raw":"{
  "answer_pre": "In the RPF-based Predict-then-Optimise approach, the variable being optimised is the slack variable \( u_s \) to achieve AC-feasibility. In the GAN-LSTM anomaly detector, the variable being optimised is the latent vector \( z \) for anomaly detection. The frozen-network optimisation is feasible in both frameworks because the trained neural network's parameters are kept fixed during inference, allowing the network to be reused for different tasks without retraining.",
