{"answer_pre_raw":"{
  "answer_pre": "In the RPF formulation, the inference-time optimization minimizes the residual norm \( \rho(\hat{\mathbf{v}}(\mathbf{u}), \mathbf{u}) \) \) to find the least infeasible power flow \( \mathbf{v}^* \). In the Predict-then-Optimize (PO) approach, the inference-time optimization minimizes the objective function \( f(\mathbf{u}) + \lambda \rho(\hat{\mathbf{v}}(\mathbf{u}), \mathbf{u}) \) to find the optimal control inputs \( \mathbf{u}^* \).",
