{"answer_pre_raw":"{
  "answer_pre": "In both papers, the truncation-and-tail-estimate technique is used to bound a combinatorial sum by splitting it into a finite sum (truncation) and an estimated tail (tail estimate). The truncation provides a lower or upper bound on the sum, and the tail estimate bounds the remaining part of the sum. This technique is valid because the truncation captures the main contribution of the series/product, and the tail estimate provides a rigorous bound on the remainder, ensuring the overall bound is tight.",
  "evidence_pages": [
    2,
    6
  ]
