{"answer_pre_raw":"{
  "answer_pre": "The structural difference is that Burde's analysis focuses on the exact unimodality of the function p(n,k) for fixed n and varying k, identifying a sharp turning point at k(n), whereas Holdum-Klausen-Rasmussen's analysis deals with the asymptotic behavior of the set of numbers not satisfying a conjecture related to central binomial coefficients, leading to a density result rather than a precise finite threshold.",
