{"answer_pre_raw":"{
  "answer_pre": "In the seismic MCMC sampler, the mixing-weight/exact-observation-count threshold is determined by the number of exact image observations. When the number of exact image observations matches the number of unknown elements in the effective blur kernel, the posterior distribution stabilizes, indicating a transition to concentration on a single deterministic answer. In the history-inference framework, the concentration parameter Θ governs the trade-off between exploration and exploitation. When Θ is small, the Gibbs sampler may struggle to jump between modes, while a larger Θ allows for better exploration of the multimodal solution space.",
  "evidence_pages": [
    "Doc 1",
    "Doc 2"
  ]
