{"answer_pre_raw":"```json
{
  "answer_pre": "In the seismic semi-blind deconvolution posterior, exact/endpoint observational constraints are used to prevent sign-shift multimodality by constraining the solution to match the observed data. In the Bayesian history-inference framework, similar constraints are applied to avoid metastable MAP histories, leading to a more constrained solution set.",
  "evidence_pages": [
    "Doc 1",
    "Doc 2"
