{"answer_pre_raw":"{
  "answer_pre": "The requirement for pre-computed hierarchical clustering in graph neural network pooling restricts the model to a fixed hierarchical structure prior to training, whereas parameter inference in binary gene regulation models involves learning the hierarchical structure during training. This pre-computed approach simplifies the analysis of large-scale gene regulatory networks by avoiding the need to infer the hierarchical structure on-the-fly, thus enhancing computational tractability.",
