{"answer_pre_raw":"```json
{
  "answer_pre": "Both papers address the challenge of distinguishing between transient anomalies and persistent structural features by employing robust statistical methods. EWMAD-DT differentiates between abrupt and incremental drifts through a dual-channel decision process, while the asymmetric Laplace distribution (ALDRM) handles extreme values by modeling location, scale, and shape parameters. EWMAD-DT uses a dual-channel decision process to distinguish between point outliers and concept drifts.",
  "evidence_pages": [
    1,
    2
  ]
}
