{
  "answer_pre": "LARGE uses a single global tuning parameter λ_j for each component X_j, while RLGP uses a single hyperparameter q that controls the sparsity of the outlyingness function. RLGP's q is robust to outliers and discontinuities, whereas LARGE's λ_j adapts to local noise and heterogeneity.",
