{"answer_pre_raw":"{
  "answer_pre": "The Linfoot informational correlation is invariant to monotone transformations of the underlying variables due to its definition as a transformation of mutual information, which is invariant to strictly monotone transformations. Chatterjee's rank correlation is invariant to continuous injective transformations of the underlying variables, as it arises naturally as an ε→0 limit of a local averaging construction. Thus, the Linfoot correlation tolerates strictly monotone transformations, while Chatterjee's rank correlation tolerates continuous injective transformations.",
