{"answer_pre_raw":"{
  "answer_pre": "The GMQ approach leverages global convexity for gradient-based optimization, enabling efficient gradient descent methods like Barzilai-Borwein descent, which is suitable for fast point estimation. In contrast, ALDRM relies on a likelihood-based Gaussian mixture representation for full distributional/Bayesian inference, making it well-suited for comprehensive probabilistic modeling.",
