{"answer_pre_raw":"{
  "answer_pre": "When the skewness parameter is fixed, the location parameter is interpreted as both a quantile and a distributional characteristic. However, when the skewness parameter is modeled as a function of covariates, the location parameter is only interpreted as a quantile. This implies that modeling the skewness parameter as a function of covariates allows for studying the effect of covariates on central tendency by isolating the impact of skewness on the location parameter.",
