{"answer_pre_raw":"{
  "answer_pre": "The entropy-constrained Gaussian channel's capacity approaches its limiting value exponentially fast (exponentially in SNR) with SNR, exhibiting an O(sqrt(SNR)) second-order penalty. In contrast, the perfect one-cold Poisson channel's capacity approaches its limiting value exponentially fast with duration T, avoiding an O(sqrt(T)) second-order penalty when measured on a comparable dispersion scale.",
  "evidence_pages": [
    3,
