{"answer_pre_raw":"{
  "answer_pre": "In the first paper, discreteness enables the use of a discrete Gaussian distribution with large minimum distance between atoms for high SNR capacity-achieving distributions. In the second paper, discreteness allows for a one-cold tree structure where each node has a finite number of children, enabling efficient encoding by grouping values into bands. The specific spacing/partition property (large minimum distance in the first paper, finite children per node in the second) drives optimality.",
