{"answer_pre_raw":"{
  "answer_pre": "The shared separation criterion is the minimum distance between consecutive atoms in the input distribution. For the entropy-constrained Gaussian channel, this is achieved by a discrete Gaussian distribution with atoms equally spaced on a scaled integer lattice. For the one-cold Poisson channel, the optimal non-asymptotic code uses an L-ary one-cold tree structure to group values into bands, exploiting region disjointness.",
