{"answer_pre_raw":"{
  "answer_pre": "Both papers formalize the deviation of average miscoverage from the target level with a term that shrinks as the number of observed test points N grows, while the echocardiogram subgroup study reports confidence intervals that widen as subgroup patient counts shrink. Using the specific bound and specific interval widths reported, both papers formalize the same underlying statistical dependency on sample size, and what this implies about interpreting either paper's small-sample subgroup/segment results as evidence of a real effect.",
  "evidence_pages": [16]
