{"answer_pre_raw":"{
  "answer_pre": "The shared method involves constructing a special function based on distance to a hypersurface and comparing it against a model-space solution using a comparison inequality derived from curvature/geometry bounds. The key structural difference lies in the derivation of the comparison inequality: the first paper (Doc 1) derives the inequality by leveraging properties of the distance function and the geometry of the hypersurface, while the second paper (Doc 2) uses a different approach involving convex barriers and angular control to establish the inequality.",
  "evidence_pages": [1, 2]
