{"answer_pre_raw":"{
  "answer_pre": "The first paper avoids the combinatorial complexity inherent in discrete-time approaches by reformulating the switched optimal control problem as a continuous embedded optimal control problem (MEOCP), enabling the use of conventional continuous optimal control solvers like GPOPS-II without requiring problem-specific modifications. The second paper avoids the fixed time discretization and iterative updates required by the mode insertion gradient (MIG) method, instead reformulating the switched optimal control problem as a continuous embedded optimal control problem (MEOCP), eliminating the need for explicitly tracking switching events and sequences.",
