{"answer_pre_raw":"{
  "answer_pre": "The ARLF robust regression learner and the GMQ quantile loss function both use a single scalar shape parameter to interpolate between distinct loss regimes, but they differ in how this parameter governs the bias-robustness tradeoff. The ARLF robust regression learner uses the shape parameter to control the trade-off between bias and robustness by adjusting the smoothness of the loss function, while the GMQ quantile loss function uses the shape parameter to control the smoothness of the loss function, which affects the balance between bias and robustness. They can be unified under the shared design criterion of using a shape parameter to control the smoothness of the loss function, which influences the bias-robustness tradeoff.",
  "evidence_pages": [
